    const Section(
      title: '+ Develop a practical college readiness plan addressing medical self-management, emergency preparedness, and healthcare access at the college location.',
      content: '**College Readiness — Medical Self-Management Plan**:\n\n**Self-Management Skills Checklist** (assess and train before departure):\n- [ ] Independent CIC via Mitrofanoff on schedule, including in unfamiliar settings (public restrooms, dorm bathroom)\n- [ ] Independent bowel program execution including suppository insertion and digital stimulation\n- [ ] Ordering and managing catheter and bowel supply inventory (insurance, DME company contact)\n- [ ] Recognizing UTI symptoms vs. asymptomatic bacteriuria (when to treat vs. when to monitor)\n- [ ] Daily skin checks of all insensate areas with hand mirror\n- [ ] Medication management (refills, pharmacy transfer, insurance authorization)\n- [ ] Recognizing VP shunt malfunction symptoms (headache, nausea, vision changes, cognitive decline)\n- [ ] Weight management strategies and accessible exercise options\n- [ ] Wheelchair maintenance: tire inflation, caster replacement, frame adjustment\n- [ ] KAFO inspection and minor troubleshooting\n\n**Emergency Preparedness Plan**:\n- Identify the nearest Level 1 trauma center and neurosurgery service (for shunt emergencies)\n- Identify a urologist near campus familiar with neurogenic bladder\n- Medical alert identification (bracelet or app-based) listing: latex allergy (life-threatening), VP shunt, myelomeningocele, neurogenic bladder\n- Emergency wallet card with medical passport summary, neurosurgery contact, and family emergency contact\n- Educate roommate on latex allergy recognition and epinephrine auto-injector use (prescribe EpiPen if latex allergy confirmed)\n- Register with campus security/disability services for emergency evacuation assistance\n\n**Healthcare Access at College**:\n- Establish with an adult PM&R physician, urologist, and primary care physician near campus BEFORE departure\n- Transfer medical records and baseline imaging to new providers\n- Ensure insurance coverage extends to the college location (network considerations)\n- Campus health center: Visit before classes start, provide medical passport, educate staff on spina bifida, confirm latex-free exam rooms\n- Pharmacy: Transfer prescriptions, ensure specialty supplies (catheters, suppositories) can be delivered to campus address\n\n**Disability Services Office**:\n- Register early (ideally spring before enrollment)\n- Accommodations to request: accessible dormitory room (roll-in shower, grab bars, adjustable bed height, proximity to accessible entrance), accessible classroom assignment, extended time for exams if bathroom breaks needed, priority course registration (to secure accessible classroom locations), accessible parking permit\n- Housing: Single room or accessible suite preferred. Ideally ground floor. Ensure bathroom accommodates wheelchair and has space for bowel program supplies.\n\n**Vocational and Academic Planning**:\n- Graphic design is an excellent career choice — compatible with physical limitations, can be done remotely\n- Vocational Rehabilitation (VR) services: State VR agency can provide funding for tuition, adaptive technology, transportation, and other supports for individuals with disabilities pursuing education or employment\n- Assistive technology assessment: Adaptive computer workstation (wheelchair-height desk, ergonomic setup to protect shoulders and wrists)\n\n**Social Integration**:\n- Encourage connecting with campus disability advocacy groups\n- Adaptive sports and recreation programs (wheelchair basketball, hand cycling club)\n- Counseling center: Establish contact early for ongoing support during transition\n- Social media advocacy: Her existing platform is a strength — connect with college disability community online\n\n**Supply Management**:\n- Catheter supplies: Order 3-month supply before departure. Establish auto-delivery. Keep 2-week emergency stock.\n- Bowel program supplies: Same approach\n- Backup wheelchair (if possible) or identify local wheelchair repair service\n- KAFO: Identify orthotist near campus for adjustments and repairs',
